1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Resume RAG: 30 synthetic resumes, 5 job descriptions, HuggingFace

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
embeddings, ChromaDB - built in VS Code.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Two entry points: resume_rag.py builds the vector store; job_matcher.py

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:38,000
retrieves, scores, and enforces must-haves.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Resumes are chunked by section, not by character count - Skills, Experience,

6
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:04,000
and Education stay intact.

7
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Running ingestion: 30 PDFs parsed, 150 section chunks embedded, 150 records

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:24,000
stored in ChromaDB.

9
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Hybrid score: 60% semantic + 30% keyword + 10% experience. Any failed

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:52,000
must-have caps the score at 59.

11
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
contains_term() handles wording variants: REST API matches REST APIs, but

12
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
bare 'deployed' never counts.

13
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Machine Learning Engineer: Sana Khan is the only qualified candidate in the

14
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,000
top 10, at 79.91.

15
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Her evidence: deployed NLP classification models, monitored production

16
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:38,000
drift, Python, PyTorch, TensorFlow.

17
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Python Backend: 0 qualified. Aarav's REST APIs now match, but 3 years and no

18
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,000
deployment still fail.

19
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Evaluation: Precision@10 0.44, Recall@10 0.733, retrieval accuracy 44.0%,

20
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:02,000
~0.27s per job.

21
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Only 2 of 30 candidates qualify - no inflated shortlist. Code:

22
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:16,000
github.com/Rachit3021/RAG-Based-Profile-matching
